# Reactor vs XAML

Coming soon — this page is the architectural essay for XAML developers:
why the binding model is fundamentally different, with a side-by-side
mapping table from XAML concepts (DependencyProperty, Binding,
DataTemplate, Style, ResourceDictionary, VisualStateManager, Storyboard,
INotifyPropertyChanged, MVVM ViewModel) to their Reactor equivalents.
See [the AI Author Skill](../../_pipeline/ai-author-skill.md) for the
planned surface.

Complements [Reactor for XAML Developers](xaml-developers.md), which is
the migration-recipe cookbook ("I have a XAML page; rewrite it as
Reactor"). This page answers the deeper *why*. Cross-linked from
[Architecture Overview](architecture-overview.md) in the Under-the-hood
track.
